<title>NETHERLANDS: Akzo completes phosphorous chemicals plant.</title>
<headline>Akzo completes phosphorous chemicals plant.</headline>
<dateline>ARNHEM, Netherlands 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemical group Akzo Nobel NV said on Tuesday it had completed its 80 million marks investment in a phosphorous chemicals plant in the German town of Bitterfeld.</p>
<p>With production in the U.S. and Japan already in place, the German site gives Akzo Nobel a worldwide coverage in this sector, it added.</p>
<p>The site will produce phosphorous trichloride, phosphorous oxychloride and phosphorous acid. Phosphorous chemicals are used to produce flame retardants, PVC plasticisers and fire-resistant hydraulic fluids.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
